I am very sorry to hear about your friend's loss. My thoughts are with you right now. Let us share a story of someone who also experienced a loss. 

A few years ago, my friend, Sarah, was diagnosed with cancer. She had been going through chemotherapy for months but her condition worsened and she passed away on the day we were planning our funeral. It was heartbreaking to know that she would not be able to attend our gathering. 

However, it is important to remember that life goes on even when one's loved ones are no longer here. We can still celebrate their lives in other ways. For example, Sarah had a passion for gardening and decided to give back to the community by starting a garden project at her local park. Her friends and family came together to help her plant seeds, water them, and watch over her as she tended to her plants. This act of kindness has made her life more meaningful and joyful. 

In addition, Sarah enjoyed reading books and writing poetry. She started a book club at work where people could meet to discuss and enjoy her favorite authors. She also wrote a poem about her friend that was published in a literary magazine. 

These examples show how we can still live a full and happy life while being surrounded by the pain of death. The key is to embrace the love and care of those closest to us during this time. Remember, life is precious enough to cherish every moment.

Please let us know if there is anything else we can do to support you in your grief journey. Your support means the world to me. I will always love you, Sarah. 

Love,
